/*!
    \qmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \title RhythmGame QML Types
    \brief Reusable behavior and data components available to every skin.

    The module provides optional building blocks rather than a required skin
    framework. A skin can use a complete controller such as
    \l StandardSelectController, select only lower-level components, or replace
    individual actions while retaining the standard behavior for everything
    else.
*/

/*!
    \page qml-api.html
    \title QML API Reference

    These components contain reusable behavior and state. Skins remain
    responsible for presentation and may instantiate only the pieces they need.

    \section1 Selection

    \list
        \li \l StandardSelectController composes the complete standard selection behavior.
        \li \l StandardSelectState owns browsing, filtering, sorting, scores, and activation.
        \li \l StandardSelectSession owns folder contents, history, and score-query lifetime.
        \li \l StandardSelectActivation opens charts and courses.
        \li \l StandardSelectModelAdapter adapts logical entries for circular presentation.
        \li \l StandardSelectFeedback provides optional navigation sounds.
        \li \l StandardSelectInput maps keyboard and controller input.
        \li \l StandardSelectNavigation implements directional and scratch navigation.
        \li \l StandardSelectShortcuts implements selection-specific F-key shortcuts.
    \endlist

    \section1 Other screens and application behavior

    \list
        \li \l StandardMainActions provides main-menu destinations.
        \li \l StandardDecideFlow handles decide-screen lifetime and input.
        \li \l StandardResultInput handles result dismissal and retry input.
        \li \l StandardGameplayExit handles gameplay escape behavior.
        \li \l StandardGameplayAttemptState tracks whether a play was attempted.
        \li \l StandardShortcuts implements application-wide F-key shortcuts.
        \li \l StandardInputKeys classifies standard gameplay input keys.
    \endlist
*/
